# Project-owned acceptance tests

`npm run validate` remains a lightweight starter check. An empty fixture skips the
starter smoke; a malformed nonempty fixture fails. HTTP 200 alone never establishes
content or permission coverage.

The configured-project gate runs project readiness, unit tests and
`npm run test:browser -- --strict`. Strict mode consumes structured Node test events
and requires at least one executed, successful `acceptanceTest` for **every site in
the current effective catalogue**, including personal overrides. Skips, TODOs and
filtered-out cases do not count. New sites therefore require new cases. The runner
consumes `--strict`; other Node test flags still work. Its strict reporter is owned
by the runner. This is a declaration of executed acceptance coverage: the project
author remains responsible for meaningful assertions and sufficient scenarios.

Pack unit tests use `support/mirage.mjs` without a selected site and need no export.
For source-bound runners use `siteMirage(site, { config })` from `support/site.mjs`:
it imports the selected site's sources and applies platform, observed, deployment
and other runtime defaults. Pass an independent synthetic fixture catalogue in tests;
never silently bind these tests to a developer's real checkout. Start owned tests
with `port: 0`, `watch: false` and a disposable state file. Use
`attachSite(site, { config })` for an existing configured runtime, or provide its
known loopback `origin` when a dynamic runtime is not discoverable or matches are
ambiguous. The helper checks the runtime source against the selected site even
with an explicit origin. Attachment does not own the runtime: do not stop it during cleanup.

The following optional recipe can be adapted into
`test-browser/local.acceptance.test.mjs`. It creates invented sources, an independent
catalogue and ephemeral data, checks rendered content, authenticates through public
session helpers and verifies an anonymous denial. Keep the default fixture folders
empty until the project owns its assertions. Change `site` to the configured site
whose coverage this recipe represents; repeat/adapt cases for other required sites.
Only this example's own simulator is closed. No credentials or live portal are needed.

```js
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import fs from 'node:fs/promises';
import os from 'node:os';
import path from 'node:path';
import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';
import { createPortalSession } from 'paqvilo/mirage/testing';
import { runAcceptance } from 'paqvilo/mirage/acceptance';
import { acceptanceTest, siteMirage } from '../support/site.mjs';

const site = 'portal';
acceptanceTest(site, 'invented content, authenticated data and anonymous denial', async () => {
  const directory = await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'local-acceptance-'));
  let simulator, signedIn, anonymous;
  try {
    const source = path.join(directory, 'portal');
    await fs.mkdir(path.join(source, 'web-pages'), { recursive: true });
    const files = {
      'website.yml': 'adx_websiteid: fixture\nadx_name: Invented fixture',
      'Home.webpage.yml': 'adx_webpageid: home\nadx_name: Home\nadx_partialurl: /',
      'Home.webpage.copy.html': '<h1 id="fixture-title">Invented acceptance content</h1>',
      'webrole.yml': '- adx_webroleid: reader\n  adx_name: Reader',
      'sitesetting.yml': '- adx_name: Webapi/sample_item/enabled\n  adx_value: "true"\n- adx_name: Webapi/sample_item/fields\n  adx_value: sample_itemid,title',
    };
    for (const [name, body] of Object.entries(files)) await fs.writeFile(path.join(source, name), body);
    const config = path.join(directory, 'fixture.config.yml');
    await fs.writeFile(config, JSON.stringify({ sourceRoot: '.', defaultSite: site, sites: {
      [site]: { source: 'portal', defaultEnv: 'local', environments: { local: 'https://fixture.example.test' }, mirage: { port: 0, solutionRoots: [] } },
    } }));
    const mirage = await siteMirage(site, { config: pathToFileURL(config) });
    const initial = mirage.initialState();
    initial.mappings.contact = { idColumn: 'contactid' };
    initial.mappings.sample_item = { idColumn: 'sample_itemid', entitySet: 'sample_items' };
    initial.tables.contact = [{ contactid: 'fixture-contact', fullname: 'Invented Reader' }];
    initial.tables.sample_item = [{ sample_itemid: 'fixture-row', title: 'Allowed fixture row' }];
    initial.permissions = [{ id: 'reader', entity: 'sample_item', scope: 'global', roles: ['Reader'], operations: ['read'] }];
    initial.settings.permissionMode = 'enforce';
    initial.simulator.mode = 'local';
    initial.simulator.pageMode = 'local';
    initial.simulator.endpoints = [];
    initial.simulator.permissionSource = 'configured';
    initial.simulator.contactRoles = [{ contactId: 'fixture-contact', roleId: 'reader' }];
    simulator = await mirage.createSimulator({ initial, stateFile: path.join(directory, 'state.json'), port: 0, watch: false });
    const blocked = new Set();
    const result = await runAcceptance({ localUrl: simulator.url, outputDir: path.join(directory, 'evidence'),
      prepareContext: async context => {
        // Apply before any page opens. Unexpected HTTP(S) assets cannot escape CI.
        await context.route('**/*', route => {
          const url = new URL(route.request().url());
          if (url.origin === new URL(simulator.url).origin) return route.continue();
          blocked.add(url.origin); return route.abort('blockedbyclient');
        });
      },
      flows: [{ name: 'Expected rendered content', steps: [
        { action: 'navigate', path: '/' },
        { action: 'text', selector: '#fixture-title', value: 'Invented acceptance content' },
      ] }],
    });
    assert.equal(blocked.size, 0, 'unexpected external requests fail hermetic acceptance');
    assert.equal(result.passed, true, 'rendered content and browser requests must pass');
    signedIn = await createPortalSession({ origin: simulator.url, contactId: 'fixture-contact' });
    const allowed = await signedIn.json('/_api/sample_items');
    assert.equal(allowed.status, 200, 'authenticated fixture read must succeed');
    assert.deepEqual(allowed.body.value.map(row => row.title), ['Allowed fixture row']);
    anonymous = await createPortalSession({ origin: simulator.url });
    assert.equal((await anonymous.json('/_api/sample_items')).status, 403, 'anonymous fixture read must be denied');
  } finally {
    try { signedIn?.close(); anonymous?.close(); }
    finally { try { await simulator?.close(); } finally { await fs.rm(directory, { recursive: true, force: true }); } }
  }
});
```

Hermetic browser tests must reject unexpected external requests, including exported
scripts, styles, images, frames and fetches. `confinePortalPages` is useful for local
navigation but is not a promise that every authored asset stays offline. Keep live
reference comparisons and shell capture explicitly selected and authorized.
